Carafe: installing a hook flushes the instruction cache only for the bytes it changed and for its trampoline.
A flush with no address means the whole process; on x86 it costs nothing, but FEX throws away every block it has
translated, so each of the hooks dxwrapper installs while a program's threads already run made them translate
their code again: loading dxwrapper from a running program took over a minute.
Zlib, as the file it changes.

--- a/DDrawCompat/v0.3.2/Common/Hook.cpp
+++ b/DDrawCompat/v0.3.2/Common/Hook.cpp
@@ -168,7 +168,8 @@
 		VirtualProtect(targetFunc, src - targetFunc, PAGE_EXECUTE_READ, &oldProtect);
 
 		origFuncPtr = trampoline;
-		CALL_ORIG_FUNC(FlushInstructionCache)(GetCurrentProcess(), nullptr, 0);
+		CALL_ORIG_FUNC(FlushInstructionCache)(GetCurrentProcess(), trampoline, trampolineSize);
+		CALL_ORIG_FUNC(FlushInstructionCache)(GetCurrentProcess(), targetFunc, src - targetFunc);
 
 		HMODULE module = nullptr;
 		GetModuleHandleEx(GET_MODULE_HANDLE_EX_FLAG_FROM_ADDRESS | GET_MODULE_HANDLE_EX_FLAG_PIN,
